# Enclosure Health LLM Guide

Use this as the default preflight and post-change verification.

## When To Run

- Before making changes, after reading `.enclosure/` guidance.
- After changes, before summarizing results to the user.
- When one command should cover workspace and architecture health.
- Last in automation after `enclosure workspace rules` and `enclosure workspace recipe --check`.

## How To Interpret

- Use `--v` for quick status, `--vv` for normal preflight, and `--vvv` for detail.
- Treat this as root rollup. Use `enclosure workspace health` and `enclosure architecture health` for detail.
- Error findings are blocking; name the follow-up command.
- Workspace findings point to `enclosure workspace health`, `enclosure workspace rules`, or `enclosure workspace recipe --check`.
- Architecture findings point to `enclosure architecture health`, then focused checks.
- Passing root health does not replace relevant tests.
